Subject: fmha bwd: prepare workspace metadata on-device (HIP-graph capturable)

The ck_tile launcher stages the bwd workspace metadata -- nsplits[]/offsets[] and,
for group+deterministic, the per-batch FmhaBwdBatchState array -- through a host
callback with pinned-host staging and a metadata D2H/H2D round trip, which is
illegal under HIP graph capture. Replace it with a tiny single-thread kernel that
writes the same metadata straight into the device workspace, so the whole bwd path
is stream-ordered and capturable.

Ported from ROCm/rocm-libraries branch zain/ck/prep-workspace-device:
  8a49132 [CK_TILE] Prepare FMHA BWD workspace metadata on-device
  b9c2588 Added backwards-compat and group-mode metadata filling

